            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Louanne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great seasoning, I put it on haddock with fresh lemon juice and grilled it in aluminum foil!! Wonderful addition to my \"homemade seasonings\". FYI if you like this one try cajun spice mix listed on this site!! Enjoy"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mark N Naomi McKenzie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Was really good and my husband loved it! Even my kids ate it. I didn't have quite all the seasonings (Rosemary, celery salt, or oregano), but went by the recipe on the ones I had and it was perfect. I did use lemon pepper instead of black, and added a tiny bit of crushed red pepper and paprika. I will definitely use this over and over again. Thank you!\n\nNote: I dipped the fish in a egg/milk mixture, and than coated in plain breadcrumbs with some of the seasoning mixed into it, then fried it in margarine. DELICIOUS!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-18T07:07:07.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carlo Elstak"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was looking to replace the fish seasoning that I used to buy at Davison's Farms in Vernon. This is definitely it!!. Rubbed it on with some lemon juice and a bit of olive oil, then baked at 400 ° for 18 minutes....delish!!",
            "datePublished": "2021-09-08T21:46:24.727Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heidi Rose"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As written it's definitely 4 stars. To make it 5 stars, I cut the salt and rosemary in half and added 1 teaspoon lemon zest, 1/2 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes and 1/4 teaspoon paprika. It gives it a kick and a hints similar to that of Old Bay seasoning. A real keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-30T19:13:43.380Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "just_jam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "we enjoyed this blend on salmon that we grilled/smoked.. added the lemon zest, crushed red pepper, and paprika as Heidi Rose suggested and left the amounts of the original ingredients the same.. only substituting kosher salt for the sea salt and celery seed for the celery salt.. ty for the recipe",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-24T15:04:49.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "eawcook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love to cook with herbs-so good for you. I made this with just a pinch of rosemary (I find the flavor too strong), half the salt, and a few pinches of dill. THEN, I added the sauce from the \"Sauced Fish\" recipe on this website (just use less lemon.) Baked till flaky and it was delicious! Had a nice herb flavor with just the right amount of zip from the sauce. Try it!",
            "datePublished": "2013-11-24T14:30:02.530Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "linda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Mixed this up tonight to put on some salmon - Oops - did not have the sage or marjoram, so I doubled the rosemary- garlic blend I had and added some dry mustard. Excellent!! Smells just like the stuff in bottles that sells for $4-6 each!! Will use again for sure!!! Thanks!!!",
            "datePublished": "2015-03-13T16:08:49.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scotdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was great. I used it with a bit of oil on my salmon. Very easy, flavorful fish. I did use less Rosemary (not a huge fan of it) and sea salt since we have to eat low sodium. I only have celery flakes so I used those. It was great &amp; I'll be using it in lots of recipes. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-30T15:15:41.090Z"
          },
          {
